One strategy (besides those mentioned) that I've found useful
on low levels to deal with nymphs:

You have to still have your pet with you for this to work.
 
First, drop all weapons, armor, etc.  (You may want to map out
the entire level first to clear most of the native monsters.)
 
Then, take your pet and go after the nymph, attacking it with
your bare hands.  
 
Why does this work?  If the nymph attacks you, she'll try to
steal something, find nothing, and teleport away -- but only
after you've had a chance to hit her.  If you've got your pet
with you, though, and she tries to charm your pet, you'll have
a few chances to hit the nymph before she turns to attack you.
Sometimes, after 2 or 3 teleports, I can kill her.
 
Of course, this doesn't work if you don't have a pet ...
 
